---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const HOST = 'mtg.subch.us';
const PORT = '17171';
const DISCORD = 'https://discord.gg/YOUR-INVITE-CODE';
---

<Base
  title="Commander"
  description="Play Magic: The Gathering Commander with friends on the subch XMage server. Setup, decks, and server status."
>
  <h1>Commander night</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Four-player Commander on our own server, with the rules enforced for you.
    Free, no account, and you can be in a game in about ten minutes.
  </p>

  <div class="status" id="server-status" data-state="unknown">
    <span class="dot dot-unknown" id="status-dot"></span>
    <span class="status-body">
      <strong id="status-text">Checking the server...</strong>
      <small id="status-sub">One moment</small>
    </span>
  </div>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Get set up</h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li class="step">
        <h3>Download XMage</h3>
        <p>
          XMage is a free program that plays Magic with all the rules enforced,
          so nobody has to remember how the stack works. It is a desktop app, not
          a website, so it has to be installed.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a class="btn" href="https://xmage.today/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            Download XMage
          </a>
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Grab the <strong>full</strong> download, around 250&nbsp;MB.</li>
          <li>Unzip it anywhere, then run <code>run-LAUNCHER.cmd</code> (Windows) or the <code>XMageLauncher</code> jar (Mac/Linux).</li>
          <li>The launcher sorts out Java and updates on its own. Say yes to what it offers.</li>
        </ul>
      </li>

      <li class="step">
        <h3>Connect to our table</h3>
        <p>
          In the launcher, hit <strong>Launch Client</strong>. On the connect
          screen choose <strong>Connect to another server</strong> and enter:
        </p>
        <div class="connect">
          <span class="field">
            <span>Server</span><code>{HOST}</code>
            <button class="secondary" data-copy={HOST}>Copy</button>
          </span>
          <span class="field">
            <span>Port</span><code>{PORT}</code>
            <button class="secondary" data-copy={PORT}>Copy</button>
          </span>
        </div>
        <p>
          Pick any username you like and leave the password blank. There is no
          registration on our server, so whatever you type is your name for the
          night.
        </p>
      </li>

      <li class="step">
        <h3>Bring a deck</h3>
        <p>
          XMage needs a <code>.dck</code> file. Either take a ready-made deck
          from below, or paste a list you already have and we will build the file
          for you. Save it into the <code>Decks</code> folder inside your XMage
          directory, then load it when you join a table.
        </p>
      </li>

      <li class="step">
        <h3>Sit down and play</h3>
        <p>
          In the client, open <strong>Tables</strong> and create or join a game.
          Pick <strong>Commander</strong> as the format and set it to four
          players. Voice chat happens on Discord; there is also a text chat in
          the client if you would rather type.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a class="btn secondary" href={DISCORD} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Join the Discord</a>
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Pick a deck</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      Every official Commander preconstructed deck, ready to download as a
      <code>.dck</code>. Nothing to build, nothing to buy.
      <span id="deck-count">...</span> decks.
    </p>

    <div class="filters">
      <div class="colors" role="group" aria-label="Filter by colour">
        <button class="color-btn" data-color="W" title="White" aria-label="White">W</button>
        <button class="color-btn" data-color="U" title="Blue" aria-label="Blue">U</button>
        <button class="color-btn" data-color="B" title="Black" aria-label="Black">B</button>
        <button class="color-btn" data-color="R" title="Red" aria-label="Red">R</button>
        <button class="color-btn" data-color="G" title="Green" aria-label="Green">G</button>
      </div>

      <select id="filter-theme" aria-label="Filter by theme">
        <option value="all">Any theme</option>
      </select>

      <select id="filter-bracket" aria-label="Filter by bracket">
        <option value="all">Any bracket</option>
        <option value="2">Bracket 2 - Core</option>
        <option value="3">Bracket 3 - Upgraded</option>
        <option value="4">Bracket 4 - Optimized</option>
      </select>

      <input type="search" id="filter-q" placeholder="Search decks or commanders" aria-label="Search decks" />
      <button class="secondary" id="filter-reset">Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="filter-meta">
      Showing <span id="deck-shown">0</span> decks. Colours filter to decks you
      could play with <em>only</em> those colours.
    </p>

    <div class="deck-grid" id="deck-grid"></div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Convert a decklist</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      Paste a list from Moxfield, Archidekt, or plain text. We look every card up,
      check it against the things XMage refuses, and hand back a
      <code>.dck</code> that will actually load.
    </p>

    <form id="convert-form" class="convert-grid">
      <div class="convert-row">
        <input type="text" id="deckname" placeholder="Deck name" style="flex:1;min-width:12rem" />
      </div>
      <textarea
        id="decklist"
        placeholder={"1 Atraxa, Praetors' Voice\n1 Sol Ring\n1 Arcane Signet\n...\n\nOr paste with a Commander section, or Moxfield's *CMDR* markers."}
        aria-label="Decklist"
      ></textarea>
      <div class="convert-row">
        <button type="submit">Check and convert</button>
        <button type="button" class="secondary" id="convert-clear">Clear</button>
      </div>
    </form>
    <div id="convert-out"></div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Good to know</h2>

    <details class="faq">
      <summary>What are these bracket numbers?</summary>
      <p>
        Wizards' own power scale. Bracket 2 is precon level, bracket 3 is an
        upgraded deck, bracket 4 is seriously tuned. The number shown here is
        worked out from the deck's contents - how many cards from the official
        Game Changers list it plays, plus whether it does land destruction or
        chains extra turns. Agree a bracket before you shuffle up and the game
        goes better.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq">
      <summary>The server says it is down. Now what?</summary>
      <p>
        It runs from a machine at Travis's house, so it is not up around the
        clock. The status above is rechecked every few minutes and can lag a
        little, so it is worth trying the connect button anyway. If it really is
        down, shout on Discord.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq">
      <summary>XMage rejected my deck.</summary>
      <p>
        Almost always one of three things: the deck is not exactly 100 cards, a
        card sits outside your commander's colour identity, or it is on this
        server's ban list. Run the list through the converter above and it will
        tell you which, before you ever load the client.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq">
      <summary>Where do deck files go?</summary>
      <p>
        The <code>Decks</code> folder inside wherever you unzipped XMage. Drop the
        <code>.dck</code> in there and it shows up in the deck picker when you sit
        down at a table.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq">
      <summary>Do I need to buy any cards?</summary>
      <p>
        No. XMage gives you every card in the game. That is rather the point.
      </p>
    </details>
  </section>

  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/mtg/mtg.css" />
  <script type="module" src="/mtg/app.js"></script>
</Base>
